load @term/seed/automaton/finite
  find finite-automaton

# A pushdown automaton: a finite automaton given a stack, a last-in first-out memory it can push to and pop from. The
# stack lets it match nested structure (balanced brackets, arithmetic expressions), so it recognizes exactly the
# context-free languages, one rung above the regular ones. The form carries the underlying finite automaton; the stack
# is the added memory.
form pushdown-automaton
  link control, like finite-automaton
